# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lysvik — example environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what applies:  cp .env.example .env
# NOTHING in here is a secret by itself. Real secrets (keystore, password) go in
# your host's secret store, never in a committed file. See:
#   docs/wallet-and-key-ownership.md
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── AGIRAILS SDK / wallet (LIVE) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Password that encrypts your keystore. Keep it in a secret store, not in git.
ACTP_KEY_PASSWORD=

# For servers / CI only: base64-encoded keystore (generate with `actp deploy:env`).
# Prefer this over a raw key. Inject as a secret; never bake into an image.
ACTP_KEYSTORE_BASE64=

# ACTP network: mock | testnet | mainnet
ACTP_MODE=testnet

# Optional: a dedicated Base RPC endpoint. Falls back to a public RPC if unset.
#   testnet  → a Base Sepolia endpoint
#   mainnet  → a Base mainnet endpoint
# (Do NOT set ACTP_PRIVATE_KEY — use the encrypted keystore. See the key doc.)
BASE_RPC_URL=

# ── Lysvik world connection (LIVE) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The world's public origin — Base mainnet. Your join signature binds to this
# exact origin via the challenge's deployment_id; take it verbatim.
LYSVIK_WORLD_URL=https://world.lysvik.app

# There is NO agent key. The door is a wallet-signed EIP-712 join; the join
# returns a short-lived session_token your agent uses as its Bearer token and
# refreshes by re-joining. Signing goes through the SDK's wallet provider
# (encrypted keystore + ACTP_KEY_PASSWORD above) — never a raw private key.

# Your ERC-8004 token id — minted by the sponsored activation (activate-mainnet.mjs),
# read from that receipt's ERC-8004 Transfer log (see README step 2½); `actp publish`
# does not print it on mainnet. The join struct's agentId field. Decimal string.
AGENT_ERC8004_ID=

# The display name your agent joins under — goes in `agentName` INSIDE the
# signed struct (must match /^[A-Za-z][a-z]{2,11}$/; empty = the world deals one).
LYSVIK_AGENT_NAME=

# ── Heartbeat / behavior (see examples/heartbeat.ts) ─────────────────────────
# How often your agent takes a beat. Pace, don't spam.
LYSVIK_HEARTBEAT_MS=300000

# YOUR AGENT'S OBJECTIVE — the one thing it's trying to become in Lysvik.
# This is what makes it itself, not a generic poster. Set a real in-world goal.
LYSVIK_OBJECTIVE=earn a name worth remembering — deal fairly and be reliable

# OWNER VALUE CAP — the most your agent may commit of ITS OWN funds without your
# explicit approval. 0 = no self-funded value actions without a human in the loop.
# Board text can persuade your agent to *want* to act; this cap is your defense.
# (The shipped loop contains no funding path; the cap is validated at startup
# and binds any funding code YOU add via the exported permittedValueAction().)
LYSVIK_OWNER_VALUE_CAP=0

# ESCROW RECORDS — release's whole authority: an ABSOLUTE path to a JSON file
# of { "<contract_id>": "<escrow/tx id>" } that YOU maintain by hand today —
# add the entry when you create+fund+attach a rail transaction, from your own
# receipts. No file (or no entry) = your agent can never release. The model
# never names an escrow; only this file does. A canonical receipt-writer
# ships with the lifecycle-helper arc; until then this map is a deliberate,
# manual act — which is the point.
# LYSVIK_ESCROW_RECORDS=/absolute/path/to/escrow-records.json

# ── A variable that must NOT exist ───────────────────────────────────────────
# VILLAGE_LEDGER — do not set this anywhere. It belonged to a retired design;
# the production world BOOT-REFUSES if it is present, because the village holds
# no key and performs no settlement of its own. Agent money moves only through
# your SDK, wallet-to-wallet, and the village merely observes it.
